The gallery assets are a sample of what the owner expects to send to the panel:
QR codes, UI icons with transparency, brand marks, flat illustration and one
photograph. They exist so the choices ProfileImage makes are checked against
real material rather than against two convenient examples.

Supplied by the repository owner on 2026-08-12 from a working assets directory.
mascot.png was reduced from 1254x1254 and kitten.png from 1024x1024, both with
a box filter; the rest are unchanged. Original names, where they differed:

  mascot.png         general_image_0_clean-d9u1947ivfoc7388o8qg.png
  kitten.png         generated_image.png
  sparkle.png        svgviewer-png-output.png
  moments.png        朋友圈.png
  button.png         Button.png
  anime-wide.jpeg    GpCskchaoAAjOre.jpeg          reduced from 1920x1080
  anime-face.png     Gr2U811WcAA8k-I.png           reduced from 400x400
  anime-closeup.png  微信图片_20251120141330_33_45.png  reduced from 405x454

anime-wide.jpeg is kept as JPEG rather than converted: the gallery decodes
whatever it is handed, and having one asset that is not a PNG is the only
thing checking that.

loader.svg is kept here but not used: the embed pattern only takes PNGs and
nothing in this repository rasterises SVG. It is present so the sample stays
complete rather than because anything reads it.

Rights in this material have not been established, and at least two files
appear to be machine generated. The repository is GPL-3.0-or-later, so any of
these may need replacing before it is relied on. The gallery reads whatever
PNGs sit in this directory, so swapping them needs no code change.

